Added a unified store contract (`diffsync.store.contract.StoreContract`) with namespace-isolated get/set/delete and a three-state `ready()` probe (`ready`/`degraded`/`recovering`), a name-based backend registry used by the `Adapter` constructor, resilient `RedisStore` timeouts/reconnect with explicit in-memory degradation, ordered replay and automatic recovery, JSON-by-default serialization with opt-in pickle (legacy prefix-less pickle data still readable), and a `store_status` command that continuously reports backend state and recent switch events (`--demo` runs an external-dependency-free scenario). Store contract tests live in `tests/store` and use an in-process Redis double.
